1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,333
Two days after reporting 161% revenue growth,

2
00:00:02,353 --> 00:00:05,833
SpaceX fell more than 9%

3
00:00:05,853 --> 00:00:07,741
So what happened?

4
00:00:07,761 --> 00:00:11,898
The Nasdaq fell 2.6% that day. The market was weak

5
00:00:11,918 --> 00:00:15,689
But SpaceX fell more than three times as much

6
00:00:15,709 --> 00:00:20,156
Employees and investors who held shares before the IPO can't sell for a while

7
00:00:20,176 --> 00:00:23,480
That's called a lock-up, and it ended that very day

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,513
Up to 1.3 billion SpaceX shares were unlocked

9
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:31,124
About 250 trillion won, or $190 billion, became sellable at once

10
00:00:31,144 --> 00:00:35,298
At the IPO, about 5% of shares could trade

11
00:00:35,318 --> 00:00:38,931
By early December, estimates say that rises to about a third

12
00:00:38,951 --> 00:00:43,592
How much pressure will the December unlock add? We did the math in the full video

